@startuml
title "Song Mood Storage, Retrieval, and Search - System Architecture"

skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false

actor "End User" as EndUser
actor "Operator / Data Inspector" as Operator

rectangle "Dockerized Multi-Tier Application" {
  component "React Frontend\n[Container: frontend]\nBrowser-accessible UI" as Frontend
  component "FastAPI Backend\n[Container: backend]\nSong lookup & storage workflows" as Backend
  database "Elasticsearch\n[Container: elasticsearch]\nAuthoritative song & mood store" as Elasticsearch
  component "Kibana\n[Container: kibana]\nAuxiliary data inspection UI" as Kibana
}

rectangle "External Systems" {
  component "Genius API\nExternal song search service" as Genius
}

EndUser --> Frontend : HTTP browser access\n(UI-001, FR-001, COM-001)
Frontend --> Backend : Song lookup request\n(API-001, COM-002)
Backend --> Elasticsearch : Query / write song-mood data\n(API-002, FR-002, FR-004, FR-005, NFR-004)
Backend --> Genius : Search for missing songs\n(API-003, FR-003, COM-003, C-005)
Operator --> Kibana : Open data inspection UI\n(FR-006, UI-002)
Kibana --> Elasticsearch : Inspect stored data\n(API-004)

note right of Backend
  Known song:
  - retrieve stored mood from Elasticsearch.
  Missing song:
  - search via Genius API.
  No runtime classifier or model server
  is assumed (C-009).
end note

note bottom of Elasticsearch
  Data handled:
  - Song record: song name, SLink, lyrics, language (DR-001)
  - Artist metadata: artist name, genres, song count (DR-002)
  - Mood association: song identity + mood value (DR-003)
  Dataset scope: English songs (DR-004, C-008).
end note

@enduml
